  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      526.35,
      69.53,
      538.57,
      83.0
    ],
    "text": "3A",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRomanPSMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      48.0,
      101.53,
      542.54,
      211.0
    ],
    "text": "Each nomination should be in a separate FORM and should without fail contain the recommendation of the nominator as indicated in the next paragraph. 05. The recommendation of the nominator should not be a recommendation without reasons being assigned. It required to set out specific facts and circumstances to enable the Commission to draw its own reference to the suitability or otherwise of the person nominated for appointment to the Panel of Mediators, such as, for instance, his or her present or past occupation, the period of service or engagement in such occupations, any position or trust or responsibility held by him or her and the office, if any, held by him or her in any social service/ religious/charitable Organization, Society or Body.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRomanPSMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      48.0,
      221.53,
      542.53,
      259.0
    ],
    "text": "06. An individual or a Body, Organizations or Institution should as far as possible, refrain from making more than three nominations in respect of the same Special Mediation Board Area. However, this limitation will not apply to the District Secretaries, and Divisional Secretaries.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRomanPSMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      48.0,
      269.37,
      542.52,
      295.21
    ],
    "text": "07. All nominations should be forwarded to reach the Secretary, Mediation Board Commission, 4th Floor, Ministry of Justice\u2019s Building, No. 19, Sri Sangaraja Mawatha, Colombo 10 on or before 15th August 2025.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRomanPS-BoldMT",
      "TimesNewRomanPSMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      47.99,
      305.53,
      542.5,
      331.0
    ],
    "text": "08. The Mediation Boards Commission will, based on the basic qualifications to be checked at interview, select eligible candidates to be offered a preliminary training on Mediation skills and methods.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRomanPSMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      47.99,
      341.53,
      542.49,
      367.0
    ],
    "text": "09. Final decision in connection with any matter which is not being prevailed by the regulation stipulated in this notice is the decision made by Mediation Boards Commission at any time.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRomanPSMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      47.99,
      377.83,
      516.75,
      427.3
    ],
    "text": "T. K. Ratnasuriya, Secretary, Mediation Boards Commission.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRomanPS-BoldMT",
      "TimesNewRomanPSMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      47.99,
      449.83,
      320.38,
      523.51
    ],
    "text": "Office of the Mediation Boards Commission,4th Floor, Ministry of Justice\u2019s Building, No. 19, Sri Sangaraja Mawatha, Colombo 10,18th June, 2025.FORM \u201cA\u201d",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRomanPS-BoldMT",
